From: portare-ch <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] pipewire: floor the requested quantum at 3 ms, not 128 frames

128 frames is 4 ms at 32 kHz and 2.67 ms at 48, and the device's sink
stops at 2 ms at either rate. A sweep with clock.force-quantum found
3 ms the lowest clean at both rates with RetroArch in the graph, ten
minutes of play without an xrun. It takes the PCM's mean delay from
6.5 to 4.9 ms at 32 kHz. docs/audio-latency.md has the tables.
---
--- a/audio/drivers/pipewire.c
+++ b/audio/drivers/pipewire.c
@@ -842,15 +842,21 @@
     * measures and holds half full, and the graph's own lead of a
     * quantum or more behind it, which the process callback pulls a
     * quantum of from the ring each cycle. The quantum asked for is a
-    * quarter of the setting, floored at 128 frames; the ring, sized
+    * quarter of the setting, floored at 3 ms; the ring, sized
     * below, holds the setting and is what is reported. Asking for a
     * quantum of the whole setting, as was done, had each cycle drain
     * the whole ring - rate control sampling a full-scale sawtooth - and
     * put a whole setting's worth in the graph on top of the ring. The
     * quantum is a request; the graph may hold to its own. */
+   /* The floor is a time, not 128 frames: 128 is 4 ms at 32 kHz and
+    * 2.67 ms at 48, and the device's sink stops at 2 ms at either rate.
+    * Swept with clock.force-quantum on the Nova, 60 s a value, 3 ms was
+    * the lowest clean at both rates with this frontend in the graph and
+    * ran ten minutes under play without an xrun; it takes the PCM's mean
+    * delay from 6.5 to 4.9 ms at 32 kHz. */
    buf_samples = (uint64_t)latency * rate / 4000;
-   if (buf_samples < 128)
-      buf_samples = 128;
+   if (buf_samples < (uint64_t)rate * 3 / 1000)
+      buf_samples = (uint64_t)rate * 3 / 1000;
    pw_properties_setf(props, PW_KEY_NODE_LATENCY, "%" PRIu64 "/%u", buf_samples, rate);
    pw_properties_setf(props, PW_KEY_NODE_RATE, "1/%d", rate);
    audio->stream = pw_stream_new(audio->pw->core, PW_RARCH_APPNAME, props);
